Fillets: the face of an extension rolling on its face's own surface has
its seam out of the ball's way (mitcad#239).

Past the end of a spine, where a contact leaves its face with no face
beyond, the blend rolls on the face's own surface, unbounded (0076): a
face is made of the whole surface within its natural bounds. On a
cylinder, cone, sphere or torus those bounds put the surface's seam at
parameter 0, an edge with no vertices (its other parameter runs to
infinity on a cylinder). Where the ball, leaving the face, heads for that
seam close by (a small convex arc whose circle starts 0.08 radians before
the arc, after a kink from a big arc, both rounded: the blend of the small
arc is extended back past the kink for the corner), the walk stopped on
the seam: ChFi3d_FilCommonPoint took the vertices of an edge that has none
(Standard_NullObject), and the faces around it were looked for in the
shape's maps, which do not hold that face (FindFromKey).

- ChFi3d_BuildPlane: where the ball leaves the face (across the end of the
  face's parameter range nearer the point) towards a seam of the natural
  bounds less than a quarter period away, the bounds are taken half a
  period on (the seam opposite) and the point within them. Otherwise the
  face is the one before: other bounds, or a point moved by a period where
  the ball does not cross the seam, would part the extension's parameters
  from those of the walk on the face before it.

